"text":"கிளி","lemma":"kiḷi","gloss":"parrot"}],"gloss":"parrots"},{"surface":"ஓப்பியும்","parts":[{"text":"ஓப்பு","lemma":"ōppu","gloss":"scare away"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"and/even"}],"gloss":"and chasing away"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"morning"}],"gloss":"morning"},{"surface":"வந்து","parts":[{"text":"வந்து","lemma":"வந்து","gloss":"coming"}],"gloss":"coming","split_unverified":true},{"surface":"மாலை","parts":[{"text":"மாலை","lemma":"mālai","gloss":"evening"}],"gloss":"evening"},{"surface":"பொழுதில்","parts":[{"text":"பொழுது","lemma":"poḻutu","gloss":"time"},{"text":"இல்","lemma":"il","gloss":"locative suffix"}],"gloss":"at the time"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"நல்","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"nal","gloss":"good"}],"gloss":"good"},{"surface":"அகம்","parts":[{"text":"அகம்","lemma":"akam","gloss":"heart"}],"gloss":"heart"},{"surface":"நயந்து","parts":[{"text":"நய","lemma":"nay","gloss":"desire"},{"text":"ந்","lemma":"n","gloss":"sandhi"},{"text":"த்","lemma":"t","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"உ","lemma":"u","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"desiring"},{"surface":"தான்","parts":[{"text":"தான்","lemma":"tāṉ","gloss":"himself"}],"gloss":"himself"},{"surface":"உயங்கி","parts":[{"text":"உயங்கு","lemma":"uyaṅku","gloss":"languish"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"verbal participle suffix"}],"gloss":"languishing"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"சொல்லவும்","parts":[{"text":"சொல்","lemma":"col","gloss":"speak"},{"text":"அ","lemma":"a","gloss":"infinitive suffix"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even"}],"gloss":"even to speak"},{"surface":"ஆகாது","parts":[{"text":"ஆகாது","lemma":"ākātu","gloss":"not possible"}],"gloss":"not possible"},{"surface":"அஃகியோனே","parts":[{"text":"அஃகு","lemma":"aḥku","gloss":"shrink"},{"text":"இ","lemma":"i","gloss":"past tense"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ōṉ","gloss":"he who"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"clitic"}],"gloss":"he has shrunk"}]}],"literal":"A young male elephant with sprouting tusks, desiring a young female elephant, / approaching the hill, as the hill-dwellers shout, / cleaves through the village common ground, O friend, of such a land is the lord! / Giving a garland of blue water-lilies from the mountain pool, / and helping to chase away the parrots alighting near the millet field, / coming in the morning, and in the evening time, / desiring her good heart, languishing himself, / unable even to speak, he has shrunk!","translation":"O friend! The lord of the land where a young male elephant with sprouting tusks, desiring a young female elephant, approaches the hill, and as the hill-dwellers shout, cleaves through the village common ground—he came in the morning, gave a garland of blue water-lilies from the mountain pool, helped to chase away the parrots from the millet field, and now, in the evening, desiring your good heart, he languishes, unable even to speak, and has shrunk in grief.","modern":"தோழி! இளமையான பெண் யானையை விரும்பிய, முளைக்கும் தந்தங்களை உடைய இளைய ஆண் யானையானது, மலையை நெருங்கி, அங்குள்ள குறவர்கள் ஆரவாரம் செய்ய, ஊர் மன்றத்தைப் பிளந்து கொண்டு செல்லும் நாட்டை உடையவன் நம் தலைவன். அவன் காலையில் வந்து, சுனைப் பூக்களாகிய குவளை மலர்களால் தொடுத்த மாலையைத் தந்தும், தினைப்புனத்தின் பக்கத்தில் வந்து விழும் கிளிகளை ஓட்டியும் நமக்கு உதவினான். ஆனால், மாலைப் பொழுதில் உன்னுடைய நல்ல நெஞ்சத்தை விரும்பி, அவனாகவே வருந்தி, தன் குறையைச் சொல்லவும் முடியாமல் வாடிப் போய்விட்டானே!","explanation":"The friend (தோழி) is speaking to the heroine (தலைவி) about the hero's (தலைவன்) distress. She describes how he came in the morning, brought a garland of blue water-lilies, and helped to scare away parrots from the millet field. Now, as evening falls, he is so overwhelmed by his love for the heroine that he is unable to speak and is wasting away in silence. The opening image of the young male elephant, which cleaves through the village common ground despite the shouts of the hill-dwellers, represents the hero's unstoppable love that overcomes all obstacles, yet he is rendered helpless and silent by his love for the heroine. This poem belongs to the Kuriñci tiṇai, representing the mountainous landscape and the theme of union and its obstacles.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}